{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_check.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nss=['M-read-queue','M-read-release','M-read-batches','M-peer-lifecycle','M-engine-order','M-bootstrap','M-transport-loss','M-send-caller','M-prefix-expectation','M-read-result-expectation']\nnew=[dict(id='M-peer-update-contract',file='internal/raft/peer.go',start_line=199,end_line=225,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='M-peer-bootstrap-entry',file='internal/raft/peer.go',start_line=51,end_line=87,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='M-update-commit',file='internal/raft/peer.go',start_line=409,end_line=433,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='M-memory-logdb',file='internal/raft/logdb_test.go',start_line=23,end_line=45,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='M-memory-append',file='internal/raft/logdb_test.go',start_line=121,end_line=142,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='M-logdb-interface',file='internal/raft/logentry.go',start_line=45,end_line=73,kind='interface_statement')]\nss += [s['id'] for s in new]\ng=dict(source_ids=ss,expectation_ids=['M-prefix-expectation','M-read-result-expectation'],binding_ids=['BI-read-release','BI-read-consumer'],derivation='Use accepted O-read-response-identity. Response signatures concatenate actual destination and both context words, one per emitted response to the independently identified origin. The prerequisite expected signature is formed from actual admitted readStatus.from/ctx before confirmation; result is formed from actual Peer.GetUpdate messages. Two distinct origins make association independent of the compared context. A released request implies exact one-response identity, while an unreleased request does not test the duty.',applicability='Stable-term leader consumes the admitted pending remote read after genuine follower heartbeat acknowledgments.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['Higher released index is permitted and not compared.','No client completion deadline or full application value is checked.'])\nleg=dict(source_ids=ss+['M-ticks','M-node-step','M-read-producer','M-forward-read','M-application-feedback'],expectation_ids=['M-read-result-expectation'],binding_ids=['BI-read-release'],derivation='Three real Peer instances use Launch(initial=true,newNode=true) with identical three-voter bootstrap addresses and NewTestLogDB. Bootstrap entries and every later update are appended and state saved before messages are scheduled, then Peer.Commit completes the handoff. The abstract application consumes actual committed bootstrap configuration entries through ApplyConfigChange and the empty election noop, then NotifyRaftLastApplied reports actual consumed indexes; there are no user writes. Tick only node 1 until natural election and drain all resulting messages. Require every peer knows leader 1, shares its term and has applied the committed current-term noop. ReadIndex on peer 2 generates and forwards A; its two actual contextual heartbeat sends fail by declared policy. All other messages, including B from peer 3 and genuine heartbeat responses, use one global FIFO queue, a stricter schedule than per-link FIFO. Source Transport.send permits individual failed sends (including full queue) and NodeHost.sendMessage does not resend failures; no Unreachable event is required for that path. Fixed contexts are legal nonzero outputs of the production context domain, not injected confirmations. After forwarded B is handled, observe both pending statuses before processing its heartbeats. Drain remaining messages through Peer.Handle and all update completions. Memory storage substitutes durability without crashes; no network/worker resources exist. No private raft mutation or test-only election override is used.',applicability='Single-threaded no-crash Peer integration harness, unchanged membership; substitutes a permitted lossy transport and synchronous abstract application for bootstrap/noop only.',unresolved=['No real transport queue saturation or client 